/**
 * Handles data access restrictions. (generated part)
 *
 * this is how the GeneratedAuthorizer works:
 * 
 * The access tables contain ids of objects that are authorized to a user.
 * There are 8 access tables. each of these access tables handle other
 * tables that needs to be authorized. for instance tlgnu_user_pool_acc
 * handles TLGNC_POOL (and all tables containing an FK to TLGNC_POOL).
 * 
 * The GeneratedAuthorizer assumes that whenever a table contains an fk with
 * an attribute matching the id of any of these authorized tables, access needs
 * to be restricted.
 * 
 * The gerneral rule in logon access restriction is this: if a user has no
 * entries in an access table then all data from respective tables can be 
 * accessed. If the access table contains one and more entries for a user,
 * then access to respective tables will be restricted, that is: only IDs
 * matching entries in the access table for a user will be shown from a
 * given table (if it contains a restricted ID)
 *
 * Achtung! the following entities/tables are *NOT* handled by this Authorizer:
#foreach ($ex in $excludedClasses)
